    <IRMAACalculatorMultiYear client:load />
  </div>

  <NoSignupStatement />


  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       3. PLAIN-LANGUAGE EXPLANATION
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="irmaa-section" aria-labelledby="explanation-heading">
    <h2 id="explanation-heading">What Your IRMAA Calculation Means and Why It Matters</h2>

    <p>
      IRMAA stands for <strong>Income-Related Monthly Adjustment Amount</strong>. It is a mandatory surcharge added on top of your standard Medicare Part B and Part D premiums if your income exceeds federal threshold limits.
    </p>

    <h3>The 2-Year Lookback Rule</h3>
    <p>
      Social Security determines your IRMAA status using your Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI) from your tax return <strong>two years prior</strong>. For example:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your <strong>2024 tax return</strong> (filed in 2025) determines your <strong>2026 Medicare IRMAA surcharge</strong>.</li>
      <li>Your <strong>2025 tax return</strong> (filed in 2026) will determine your <strong>2027 Medicare IRMAA surcharge</strong>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Understanding 2026 IRMAA Brackets</h3>
    <p>
      In 2026, the standard Part B premium is <strong>{STANDARD_PART_B_2026}/month</strong>. If your MAGI exceeds <strong>$106,000</strong> (Single) or <strong>$212,000</strong> (Married Filing Jointly), you enter Tier 1 of IRMAA. As your income increases across higher brackets, your monthly Part B surcharge increases up to $486.90/month, and your Part D surcharge increases up to $85.80/month.
    </p>

    <div class="irmaa-info-box">
      <p class="irmaa-info-box-heading">Key Rule: IRMAA Brackets are Cliff Thresholds</p>
      <p>
        Unlike federal income tax brackets (where only income above the bracket is taxed at the higher rate), IRMAA uses "cliff" thresholds. Going just $1 over a threshold pushes your entire monthly premium into the higher tier for the full calendar year.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       4. WORKED EXAMPLE (STEP BY STEP)
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="irmaa-section irmaa-section--tinted" aria-labelledby="worked-example-heading">
    <h2 id="worked-example-heading">Step-by-Step Worked Example: Arthur and Evelyn</h2>
    <p>
      Here is how the <strong>medicare irmaa calculator</strong> estimates IRMAA surcharges for a couple transitioning into retirement.
    </p>

    <div class="irmaa-example-card">
      <div class="irmaa-example-scenario">
        <span class="irmaa-example-label">Scenario</span>
        <p>
          <strong>Arthur &amp; Evelyn</strong> file taxes Married Filing Jointly. In <strong>2024</strong> (two years prior), Arthur sold an investment property before retiring, resulting in a joint MAGI of <strong>$285,000</strong>. In <strong>2025</strong>, with Arthur fully retired, their joint MAGI dropped to <strong>$180,000</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="irmaa-example-steps">
        <li>
          <strong>Determine 2026 IRMAA Status (2024 MAGI = $285,000):</strong>
          Comparing $285,000 Joint MAGI to 2026 CMS brackets places them in <strong>Tier 2</strong> ($266,001 to $332,000 Joint).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Calculate 2026 Monthly Surcharges per Person:</strong>
          Part B Tier 2 Surcharge = <strong>+$202.90/mo</strong> per person.<br />
          Part D Tier 2 Surcharge = <strong>+$35.30/mo</strong> per person.<br />
          Total added per person = <strong>$238.20/month</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Combined Couple Annual Cost for 2026:</strong>
          $238.20 × 2 spouses = $476.40/month total = <strong>$5,716.80 per year</strong> in extra surcharges.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Projected 2027 Status (2025 MAGI = $180,000):</strong>
          With their post-retirement income of $180,000 below the $212,000 Joint threshold, their 2027 IRMAA drops to <strong>$0 (Tier 0 Standard)</strong>, saving them $5,716.80 annually.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Action Step (Form SSA-44):</strong>
          Because Arthur's retirement was a qualifying Life-Changing Event, Arthur and Evelyn can file <strong>Form SSA-44</strong> in 2026 to request that Social Security use their 2025 lower income immediately, eliminating the 2026 surcharge.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div style="background: #fff8f0; border-left: 4px solid #E8761A; border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 700; color: #E8761A; margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;">💡 Pro Tip</p>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #0D2137; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">Run this calculator BEFORE making large IRA withdrawals or Roth conversions. A single large distribution can push your MAGI over an IRMAA cliff threshold and cost you hundreds per month in extra premiums — permanently, for that year.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       5. COMMON PITFALLS
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="irmaa-section" aria-labelledby="pitfalls-heading">
    <h2 id="pitfalls-heading">Common Medicare IRMAA Mistakes and How to Avoid Them</h2>

    <h3>Forgetting That SSA Uses a Two-Year-Old Tax Return</h3>
    <p>Many people calculate their current income and are confused when their IRMAA bracket doesn't match. SSA uses the IRS data from 2 years ago (2024 taxes determine 2026 IRMAA).</p>
    <p>The fix is <a href="https://www.ssa.gov/benefits/medicare/irmaa.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">if your income dropped significantly, file Form SSA-44 to appeal using a more recent estimate</a>.</p>

    <h3>Not Adding Municipal Bond Interest to Your MAGI</h3>
    <p>Tax-exempt municipal bond interest is added back to your AGI for IRMAA purposes (Form 1040 Line 2a). Forgetting this is the #1 surprise that pushes retirees into a higher tier.</p>
    <p>The fix is <a href="/tools/magi-for-medicare-calculator/">use our MAGI calculator to compute your correct MAGI before checking this calculator</a>.</p>

    <h3>Missing the 60-Day Appeal Window After an IRMAA Determination</h3>
    <p>If you receive an IRMAA notice and have experienced a qualifying life-changing event (retirement, divorce, death of spouse), you can appeal using Form SSA-44. But you must file within 60 days of the notice.</p>
    <p>The fix is <a href="https://www.ssa.gov/benefits/medicare/irmaa.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">contact SSA at 1-800-772-1213 or visit ssa.gov immediately upon receiving the determination letter</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
